  "sections": [
    {
      "section_title": "Q.1 Choose the correct option of the following (Any seven question\n                    only):",
      "total_marks": 14,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q1_1",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>The language \\( \\{a^m b^n c^{m+n} / m, n \\ge 1\\} \\) is</p>",
          "options": [
            "regular",
            "context-free but not regular",
            "Context-sensitive but not context free",
            "type-0 but not context sensitive"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_2",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following pairs have DIFFERENT expressive powers?</p>",
          "options": [
            "Deterministic finite automata (DFA) and non-deterministic finite automata (NDFA)",
            "Deterministic push-down automata (DPDA) and non-deterministic push-down automata (NDPDA)",
            "Deterministic single-tape Turing machine and non-deterministic single-tape Turing machine",
            "Single-tape Turing machine and multi-tape Turing machine"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_3",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>The logic of pumping lemma is a good example of</p>",
          "options": [
            "pigeon-hole principle",
            "divide-and-conquer technique",
            "recursion",
            "iteration"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_4",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>If \\( L_1 \\) and \\( L_2 \\) are context free languages, \\( L_1 - L_2 \\) is</p>",
          "options": [
            "always context-free.",
            "sometimes",
            "never",
            "None of these"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_5",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>_____ is the acyclic graphical representation of a grammer.</p>",
          "options": [
            "Binary tree",
            "Octtree",
            "Parse tree",
            "None of the above"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_6",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following pairs of regular expressions are equivalent?</p>",
          "options": [
            "\\( x^* \\) and \\( x^*x \\)",
            "\\( 1(01) \\) and \\( (10)^*1 \\)",
            "\\( x(xx)^* \\) and \\( (xx)^*x \\)",
            "All of the above"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_7",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>The maximum number of states of a DFA converted from an NFA with \\( n \\) states is</p>",
          "options": [
            "\\( n \\)",
            "\\( n^2 \\)",
            "\\( 2^n \\)",
            "None of these"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_8",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Definition of a language L with alphabet {a} is given as \\( L = \\{a^{nk} / k &gt; 0 \\}, \\) and n\n                        is\n                        a\n                        positive integer constant. What is the minimum number of states needed in a DFA to recognize L?\n                    </p>",
          "options": [
            "\\( k + 1 \\)",
            "\\( n + 1 \\)",
            "\\( 2n + 1 \\)",
            "\\( 2k + 1 \\)"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 3,
            "freq": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_9",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>A _____ is context free grammar with atmost one non-terminal in the right handside of the\n                        production.\n                    </p>",
          "options": [
            "linear grammar",
            "linear bounded grammar",
            "regular grammar",
            "None of the above"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_10",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Let N be an NFA with \\( n \\) states and let M be the minimized DFA with \\( m \\) states\n                        recognizing\n                        the same language. Which of the following is necessarily true?</p>",
          "options": [
            "\\( m \\le 2^n \\)",
            "\\( n \\le m \\)",
            "M has one accept state",
            "\\( m = 2^n \\)"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "stars": 2,
            "freq": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
